.env
.env.production
.env.local

dist/
.astro/
node_modules/

.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Camera working files. Originals belong in the asset library, not the repo —
# only the exported web asset should be committed.
*.CR3
*.xmp

# Hand-off working files — source documents you drop for me to read (lists,
# notes, exports). Whatever gets derived from them is committed as real source;
# the working file itself stays out of the repo.
_working/

# Video masters. The originals the owner supplies are 87-115MB each and are not
# what ships — public/video/ holds the web encodes made from them, and those ARE
# committed. Keeping the masters out is the same call the camera-original rule
# above makes: the source lives in the asset library, the derived web file lives
# in the repo. Re-encode with the recipe in HANDOFF.md if one needs replacing.
src/assets/home/*.mp4

# Source material the owner drops in to be read, and assets staged on disk for
# pages not yet built. Both are untracked ON PURPOSE — see the note near the end
# of HANDOFF.md, and commit 95649a7, which exists solely to record which strays
# are deliberate.
#
# They are ignored rather than merely untracked because `git add` swept them
# into four separate commits and each was unstaged by hand. That is a rule's
# job, not a reviewer's.
#
# WHEN WORK STARTS USING ONE: delete its line here and commit the file. The
# ignore is a guard against accident, not a decision that the asset is unwanted.
src/listings/*.zip
src/assets/amenities/random/
src/assets/neighborhood/origin-palms.jpg
